>     # G3_RDV: the same move on the VGPR-staged Q_PREF route, which has no LDS DMA pending to
>     # force that wait: the deferred GEMM3 runs between the WAR barrier and the publish barrier
>     # (1 = ahead of the Q/dO commit, 2 = after it), so its reads are retired by the publish
>     # drain. dS is already published by the WAR barrier: gpu.barrier lowers to a workgroup
>     # release fence + s_barrier + acquire fence, so the ds_writes retire ahead of it. With one
>     # head per kv group the producer and the deferred reader share dS slot 0, and the publish
>     # barrier is then also the WAR fence between this GEMM3's reads and this head-step's own
>     # dS writes, which otherwise only GEMM1 and the softmax separate.
